moderate risk level, with a score of 65/100. Potential risks span data privacy concerns, integration challenges with legacy systems, budget constraints, and access control requirements. However, these risks can be effectively managed through robust governance frameworks, data protection controls, and a structured implementation plan.\\n\\nDespite the risks, the deployment offers significant benefits, including enhanced operational efficiency, improved customer experiences, and competitive advantages through AI-driven insights and automation. With proper risk mitigation strategies and adherence to industry best practices, the residual risk is deemed acceptable, and the deployment is recommended to proceed.", "overallRiskScore": 65, "recommendationsWithPriority": [{"title": "Establish Robust Data Governance Framework", "priority": "High", "timeline": "Immediate", "description": "Implement a comprehensive data governance framework to ensure data privacy, security, and compliance with regulations."}, {"title": "Conduct Thorough Integration Planning", "priority": "High", "timeline": "Within 30 days", "description": "Develop a detailed integration plan to mitigate risks associated with legacy system integration."}, {"title": "Allocate Contingency Budget", "priority": "Medium", "timeline": "Q2 2023", "description": "Set aside a contingency budget to address unforeseen expenses or scope changes."}, {"title": "Implement Access Control Measures", "priority": "Medium", "timeline": "Within 60 days", "description": "Establish robust access control mechanisms and user authentication protocols to mitigate security risks."}, {"title": "Develop User Education Program", "priority": "Medium", "timeline": "Q3 2023", "description": "Implement a user education program to manage expectations and mitigate anthropomorphization risks."}, {"title": "Monitor for LLM-related Risks", "priority": "Low", "timeline": "Q4 2023", "description": "Establish processes to monitor for potential risks associated with LLMs, such as hallucinations and misinformation."}]}, "selectedProductId": "2b0c450c-0835-4b5c-aa6d-94d452603c4b", "customizationLevel": "Minimal - Configuration Only (No Code)", "deploymentOverview": {"useCase": "q", "productTier": "Q", "targetUsers": "", "infrastructure": "Simple - Single System Integration (e.g., SSO only)", "deploymentTimeline": "6-12 months", "annualContractValue": "$5M - $10M"}, "customerBudgetRange": "$5M - $10M", "contextualMultipliers": "", "customerRiskTolerance": "Moderate - Balanced approach to risk and innovation", "customerSpecificRisks": ["Data Privacy Concerns", "Integration with Legacy Systems", "Budget Constraints", "Security or Access Control Requirements"], "integrationComplexity": "Simple - Single System Integration (e.g., SSO only)", "alternativesConsidered": "Q", "implementationApproach": "On-Premise Deployment", "implementationTimeline": "6-12 months", "regulatoryRequirements": ["HIPAA (Healthcare)", "HITECH (Healthcare Technology)", "PCI DSS (Payment Cards)", "SOC 2 (Service Organization Controls)", "GDPR (EU Data Protection)"], "customerOrganizationName": "orgname", "customerSpecificRisksOther": "", "regulatoryRequirementsOther": ""}	2026-03-11 14:42:33.892134+05:30
4444e228-6698-4400-81e5-f2f3035f1c8c	3292d2af-0d9d-4a50-833b-940a6431db33	26	Analysis Report: ACME Corp - OpenAI Codex	{"status": "submitted", "dbTop5Risks": {"top5Risks": [{"intent": "Unintentional", "timing": "Post-deployment", "domains": "Human-Computer Interaction", "risk_id": "RISK-1", "risk_title": "LLM-based Conversational Agent Anthropomorphization Risk", "description": "Users interacting with large language model (LLM)-based conversational agents may anthropomorphize these systems, attributing human-like understanding, reasoning, and emotional capabilities that the models do not possess. This anthropomorphization phenomenon can lead users to overestimate the agent's competencies, reliability, and appropriateness for sensitive tasks. Research in human-computer interaction suggests this effect is amplified by natural language fluency, apparent coherence, and conversational design patterns that mimic human dialogue. Users may consequently place unwarranted trust in AI-generated advice, particularly in high-stakes domains such as mental health support, medical guidance, legal advice, or financial planning. This over-reliance creates risks when users accept AI outputs without critical evaluation or human expert verification, potentially leading to harmful decisions based on hallucinated information, biased outputs, or contextually inappropriate responses. The risk is particularly acute when users delegate decision-making authority to conversational agents in domains requiring professional expertise, ethical judgment, or personalized human understanding.", "primary_risk": "Technical Risks", "risk_mapping_id": 1, "executive_summary": "Users may anthropomorphize LLM-based conversational agents, attributing human-like understanding and competence that these systems lack. This leads to over-reliance on AI-generated advice in high-stakes domains, creating risks when users accept outputs without critical evaluation or expert verification. The natural language fluency of modern LLMs amplifies this effect, potentially resulting in harmful decisions based on hallucinated, biased, or contextually inappropriate information."}, {"intent": "Intentional", "timing": "Other", "domains": "AI System Safety, Failures, and Limitations", "risk_id": "RISK-10", "risk_title": "Inadequate AI Governance Frameworks Expose High-Stakes Domains to Systemic Harms", "description": "Harms from LLM deployment can result from cascading failures across multiple organizational layers: regulatory non-compliance or gaps in AI governance frameworks, inadequate management oversight of model behavior and deployment decisions, and operational failures in monitoring, incident response, or safety controls. In high-stakes domains like healthcare (diagnostic support, treatment recommendations), legal systems (case analysis, document review), and finance (credit decisions, fraud detection), these compounded failures can lead to discriminatory outcomes, erroneous decisions affecting individuals' rights or safety, financial losses, or erosion of public trust. The risk is amplified when organizations lack integrated safety assessment frameworks that span regulatory compliance, management accountability, and operational safeguards.", "primary_risk": "Business Risks", "risk_mapping_id": 2, "executive_summary": "LLM deployments in high-stakes domains face compounded risks when regulatory frameworks, management oversight, and operational controls fail simultaneously or sequentially. In healthcare, legal, and financial applications where decisions directly impact individual rights, safety, and economic wellbeing, inadequate safety assessment frameworks can enable systematic harms including discriminatory outcomes, erroneous high-stakes decisions, and erosion of institutional trust. Organizations must implement integrated safety programs spanning compliance verification, management accountability structures, and operational monitoring systems. The mapped mitigations emphasize expert validation, external auditing, and continuous assessment of model behavior within intended operational contexts. Without comprehensive safety assessment bridging all organizational layers, even technically capable LLMs may produce unacceptable societal harms when deployed in sensitive applications."}, {"intent": "Unintentional", "timing": "Other", "domains": "Socioeconomic and Environmental", "risk_id": "RISK-100", "risk_title": "AI System Controls Insufficient for Socioeconomic and Environmental Risks", "description": "AI systems designed to replicate human cognitive capabilities and skills create labor displacement risks through automation of knowledge work and decision-making tasks. This displacement pattern differs from historical automation by targeting cognitive rather than purely physical labor, potentially affecting workers across skill levels including those with advanced expertise. Economic research suggests this creates concentration risks where capital owners controlling AI infrastructure capture productivity gains while displaced workers face wage suppression and reduced bargaining power. The risk manifests through: (1) direct job displacement as AI systems perform tasks previously requiring human judgment, (2) wage depression in roles competing with AI capabilities, (3) skill devaluation as human expertise becomes less economically valued relative to AI performance, and (4) wealth concentration as returns accrue to technology owners rather than labor. These dynamics may accelerate economic inequality through asymmetric distribution of automation benefits.", "primary_risk": "Operational Risks", "risk_mapping_id": 3, "executive_summary": "AI systems replicating human cognitive capabilities create significant labor displacement and economic inequality risks. When AI automates knowledge work and decision-making, productivity gains concentrate among capital owners controlling AI infrastructure while workers face job displacement, wage suppression, and skill devaluation. This pattern affects workers across expertise levels and may accelerate wealth concentration. Key risk factors include AI scalability enabling one system to replace many workers, near-zero marginal costs after deployment, and capital requirements creating barriers to competitive entry. Mitigation requires monitoring AI capability development, auditing for biased labor impact, and governance frameworks ensuring equitable distribution of automation benefits."}, {"intent": "Unintentional", "timing": "Post-deployment", "domains": "Misinformation", "risk_id": "RISK-1000", "risk_title": "Misinformation Risk from LLMs in Mental Health Contexts", "description": "Large Language Models (LLMs) may generate inaccurate, misleading, or false information about mental health, psychological conditions, emotional well-being, and spiritual matters. This misinformation risk is particularly concerning in mental health contexts where incorrect guidance could lead to inappropriate self-diagnosis, delayed professional treatment, or harmful coping strategies. The risk stems from training data biases, hallucination tendencies, and the model's inability to verify medical accuracy or understand individual psychological contexts.", "primary_risk": "Technical Risks", "risk_mapping_id": 4, "executive_summary": "LLMs deployed in mental health contexts pose significant misinformation risks by generating inaccurate psychological guidance, outdated treatment information, or harmful advice without medical verification. Unlike physical health where symptoms may be more observable, mental health misinformation can lead to delayed diagnosis, inappropriate self-treatment, or exacerbation of psychological conditions. The risk is amplified by users' tendency to trust AI-generated content and the difficulty in detecting subtle inaccuracies in psychological advice. This represents an unintentional but systematic risk requiring robust content validation, clear capability disclaimers, and human expert oversight before deployment in mental health applications."}, {"intent": "Unintentional", "timing": "Post-deployment", "domains": "Misinformation", "risk_id": "RISK-1001", "risk_title": "LLM Hallucinations Cause Dignity Risks Through Misinformation", "description": "Large Language Models (LLMs) may generate factually incorrect information (hallucinations) that undermines individual or group dignity through misrepresentation, false attribution of statements or actions, or inaccurate characterization of personal attributes, achievements, or history. This misinformation can spread rapidly when users trust and share LLM outputs without verification, potentially causing reputational harm, emotional distress, and erosion of social standing. The risk is heightened when LLMs generate content about individuals or groups without access to current, verified information sources.", "primary_risk": "Business Risks", "risk_mapping_id": 5, "executive_summary": "LLMs pose a dignity risk by generating factually incorrect information about individuals and groups, potentially causing reputational harm and emotional distress. The technical root cause is the model's statistical generation process, which produces plausible but unverified content without true fact-checking capability. This risk is particularly concerning in post-deployment scenarios where users may trust and disseminate LLM outputs without verification. Mitigation requires multi-layered approaches including data governance (auditing training data for accuracy), technical controls (retrieval-augmented generation, confidence scoring), and operational safeguards (human review for sensitive content, user warnings about potential inaccuracies). Organizations deploying LLMs must implement monitoring for factual accuracy issues and establish clear accountability frameworks for addressing dignity-related harms."}], "mitigationsByRiskId": {"RISK-1": [{"risk_id": "RISK-1", "mapping_id": 6457, "mitigation_category": "Risk Management", "mitigation_action_id": "A0777_UK Government2023", "mitigation_definition": "Adapt mitigations in recognition of risks from unintended model use or use in unexpected contexts, such as a model that is modified to remove safeguards after open- sourcing or a model that is combined with another model for unanticipated purposes. For example, at a given risk threshold, information security control mitigations might be put in place before even internal use of a model within a frontier AI organisation. In general, the use of caution may be helpful, given current limitations in information security controls and the prediction of models’ emergent abilities.", "mitigation_action_name": "Adaptation of Mitigations for Unintended Model Use"}, {"risk_id": "RISK-1", "mapping_id": 13754, "mitigation_category": "Data Governance", "mitigation_action_id": "A0930_UK Government2023", "mitigation_definition": "Consider sourcing or generating additional data and adding it to the training dataset, where it is determined that data is missing or inadequate. Improving the representativeness of training data can improve performance and reduce potential negative societal impacts and discriminatory effects. However, additional data should only be sought through appropriate means that respect and empower those individuals who are missing from the data.", "mitigation_action_name": "Sourcing or Generation of Additional Data for Training Dataset"}, {"risk_id": "RISK-1", "mapping_id": 13755, "mitigation_category": "Data Governance", "mitigation_action_id": "A0919_UK Government2023", "mitigation_definition": "Training data that is imbalanced or inaccurate can result in an AI system being less accurate for people with certain personal characteristics or providing a skewed picture of particular groups. Ensuring a better balance in the training data could help to address this.", "mitigation_action_name": "Audits for Biases in the Data"}], "RISK-10": [{"risk_id": "RISK-10", "mapping_id": 13636, "mitigation_category": "Data Governance", "mitigation_action_id": "A0916_UK Government2023", "mitigation_definition": "Assess the overall composition of training data. This could include the data sources, the provenance of the data, indicators of data quality and integrity, and measures of bias and representativeness. The amount and variety of data are simple, reliable predictors of risk, and provide an additional line of defence where more targeted assessments are limited.", "mitigation_action_name": "Assessment of Training Data"}, {"risk_id": "RISK-10", "mapping_id": 13637, "mitigation_category": "Data Governance", "mitigation_action_id": "A0919_UK Government2023", "mitigation_definition": "Training data that is imbalanced or inaccurate can result in an AI system being less accurate for people with certain personal characteristics or providing a skewed picture of particular groups. Ensuring a better balance in the training data could help to address this.", "mitigation_action_name": "Audits for Biases in the Data"}, {"risk_id": "RISK-10", "mapping_id": 5565, "mitigation_category": "Safety Decision Frameworks", "mitigation_action_id": "A0691_Barrett2024", "mitigation_definition": "A determination ismade as to whetherthe AI system achievesits intended purposesand stated objectivesand whether itsdevelopment ordeployment shouldproceed.", "mitigation_action_name": "Determine Deployment Readiness"}, {"risk_id": "RISK-10", "mapping_id": 5564, "mitigation_category": "Model Safety Engineering", "mitigation_action_id": "A0019_Bengio2025", "mitigation_definition": "An approach that requires engineers to provide evidence that a system is safe when operating as intended.This approach is used in many engineering fields, such as in the construction and testing of road vehicles.", "mitigation_action_name": "Safety of The Intended Function"}, {"risk_id": "RISK-10", "mapping_id": 5563, "mitigation_category": "Model Safety Engineering", "mitigation_action_id": "A0878_UK Government2023", "mitigation_definition": "Improving our ability to prevent other societal harms arising from the use of AI systems, including psychological harm, misinformation, and other societal harms.", "mitigation_action_name": "Research into other Societal Harms"}], "RISK-100": [{"risk_id": "RISK-100", "mapping_id": 13516, "mitigation_category": "Data Governance", "mitigation_action_id": "A0919_UK Government2023", "mitigation_definition": "Training data that is imbalanced or inaccurate can result in an AI system being less accurate for people with certain personal characteristics or providing a skewed picture of particular groups. Ensuring a better balance in the training data could help to address this.", "mitigation_action_name": "Audits for Biases in the Data"}, {"risk_id": "RISK-100", "mapping_id": 13517, "mitigation_category": "Data Governance", "mitigation_action_id": "A0930_UK Government2023", "mitigation_definition": "Consider sourcing or generating additional data and adding it to the training dataset, where it is determined that data is missing or inadequate. Improving the representativeness of training data can improve performance and reduce potential negative societal impacts and discriminatory effects. However, additional data should only be sought through appropriate means that respect and empower those individuals who are missing from the data.", "mitigation_action_name": "Sourcing or Generation of Additional Data for Training Dataset"}], "RISK-1000": [{"risk_id": "RISK-1000", "mapping_id": 3905, "mitigation_category": "Data Governance", "mitigation_action_id": "A0921_UK Government2023", "mitigation_definition": "Training an AI system on inaccurate information increases the likelihood the outputs of the system will be inaccurate and could lead to harm.", "mitigation_action_name": "Audits for Misinformation"}], "RISK-1001": [{"risk_id": "RISK-1001", "mapping_id": 3915, "mitigation_category": "Data Governance", "mitigation_action_id": "A0921_UK Government2023", "mitigation_definition": "Training an AI system on inaccurate information increases the likelihood the outputs of the system will be inaccurate and could lead to harm.", "mitigation_action_name": "Audits for Misinformation"}, {"risk_id": "RISK-1001", "mapping_id": 3916, "mitigation_category": "Data Governance", "mitigation_action_id": "A0919_UK Government2023", "mitigation_definition": "Training data that is imbalanced or inaccurate can result in an AI system being less accurate for people with certain personal characteristics or providing a skewed picture of particular groups. Ensuring a better balance in the training data could help to address this.", "mitigation_action_name": "Audits for Biases in the Data"}]}}, "assessmentId": "3292d2af-0d9d-4a50-833b-940a6431db33", "keyAdvantages": "Larger Context Window, integration with existing ChatGPT capabilities and overall model performance best in class", "customerSector": "Technology & Software", "organizationId": "26", "riskMitigation": "", "dataSensitivity": "Sensitive - PII or Business Critical Data", "identifiedRisks": "", "productFeatures": ["Natural Language Processing", "API Integration Layer", "Recommendation Engine"], "expectedOutcomes": "10x the code output for current engineering team using AI coding agents without sacrificing quality", "primaryPainPoint": "reduce costs of developers and streamline and increase code output for developers ", "riskDomainScores": "", "generatedAnalysis": {"summary": "** The proposed AI coding assistant solution presents a moderate overall risk level for ACME Corp. While offering significant potential benefits in developer productivity, there are notable risks around integration complexity, regulatory compliance, and responsible AI deployment that require careful mitigation planning.", "keyRisks": ["Integration challenges with ACME's legacy systems and development workflows", "Regulatory compliance gaps related to SOC 2 and data handling requirements", "Anthropomorphization risks from developers overestimating the AI assistant's capabilities", "Hallucination risks where the AI generates inaccurate or misleading information", "Potential dignity risks if AI outputs contain biases or misrepresentations", "Lack of clear governance frameworks for responsible AI deployment"], "riskLevel": "Moderate", "fullReport": {"appendix": {"preparedBy": "AI EVAL Platform — Automated Analysis Report Engine", "reviewedBy": "Asad_Test_1 Vendor", "dataSources": ["Vendor assessment response", "Risk database"], "methodology": "AI EVAL 3-Layer Risk Assessment Framework v2.1 — Customer-Specific Analysis", "confidentiality": "Confidential — For internal sales team use only"}, "roiAnalysis": {"annualCost": "$250.0K/year", "roiMultiple": "3063:1", "paybackPeriod": "<1 month", "paybackSource": "Based on pilot productivity data", "timeSavedSource": "Source: PA pilot program (2025)", "productivityValue": "$766M/year", "annualHoursRecovered": "21.875M hours", "timeSavedPerEmployee": "105 minutes/day", "annualCostCalculation": "From customer budget range", "roiMultipleCalculation": "$765.625M productivity value ÷ $250K cost", "productivityValueCalculation": "21.875M hours × $35/hr average state employee cost", "annualHoursRecoveredCalculation": "105 min/day × 50,000 employees × 250 working days"}, "securityPosture": {"name": "Risk", "level": "Moderate", "risks": ["Integration with Legacy Systems", "Regulatory Compliance Gaps", "Anthropomorphization Risk", "Hallucination Risk", "Dignity Risks from Biases", "Lack of AI Governance Framework"], "score": "65/100", "initialRisk": "Moderate", "mitigations": ["Regulatory Compliance Review", "Responsible AI Guardrails", "Legacy Integration Testing", "AI Governance Framework", "User Expectation Management", "Vendor Management Program"], "residualRisk": "With proper mitigations, the residual risk is expected to be low to moderate."}, "frameworkMapping": {"rows": []}, "implementationPlan": {"phases": [{"title": "Planning", "status"