ption:** Develop training to set appropriate expectations on the AI assistant's capabilities. | **Timeline:** Prior to deployment", "**Priority:** Low | **Title:** Vendor Management Program | **Description:** Implement contractual and operational controls for ongoing vendor risk management. | **Timeline:** Q4 2023"], "executiveSummary": "ACME Corp is seeking to deploy an AI-powered coding assistant to dramatically increase developer output without sacrificing quality. The proposed solution leverages large language models and natural language processing to enable developers to describe requirements in plain language and receive functional code.\\n\\nKey benefits include an expected 10x increase in code output from ACME's current engineering team. This could yield substantial cost savings and accelerate product roadmaps. The vendor's offering has best-in-class performance versus alternatives evaluated.\\n\\nFrom an infrastructure perspective, the solution is delivered via SaaS with moderate customization for ACME's workflows and system integrations. Data sensitivity is moderate, involving business-critical code and potentially personal data. Regulatory requirements focus on SOC 2 controls.\\n\\nWhile the potential upside is significant, the risk assessment surfaces moderate integration complexity risks with ACME's legacy systems. There are also regulatory compliance considerations given SOC 2 requirements and the handling of sensitive data. Responsible AI risks like anthropomorphization and hallucinations from large language models must be proactively managed.\\n\\nWith an overall moderate risk profile and robust mitigation planning, the engagement carries a manageable residual risk level. We recommend proceeding with deployment while prioritizing the risk areas highlighted for mitigation.", "overallRiskScore": 65, "recommendationsWithPriority": [{"title": "Regulatory Compliance Review", "priority": "High", "timeline": "Immediate", "description": "Conduct a detailed r