772	RISK-131	A1000_Gipiškis2024	Benchmark dataset auditing	Testing & Auditing	Auditing benchmark datasets allows for verification of the utility and limitations of the datasets [158]. This allows the provider to more accurately measure AI model capabilities and safety. Auditing includes the evaluation of such datasets by independent third-party organizations and the release of benchmark dataset metadata to the auditors.
771	RISK-131	A1001_Gipiškis2024	Informative and powerful benchmarks	Testing & Auditing	Developers of GPAI systems can select benchmarks that are difficult enough to be informative about the capabilities of their AI systems, and cover a large spec- trum of domains in order to signal areas where the GPAI system is performing poorly [120].Suitable benchmarks contain no label errors, are not vulnerable to being bench- mark contaminants, and are often audited by independent domain experts if they contain domain-specific questions. For multimodal GPAI systems, good benchmarks cover every modality, especially the interaction of different modalities.
