2803	RISK-169	A0981_Gipiškis2024	Encouraging downstream provider to evaluate models for deployment-specific failure modes	Testing & Auditing	In some cases, AI system deployers are better positioned to perform certain risk management measures on the AI model in a provided AI system, relative to upstream model providers. For example, they understand their use case better and are more easily able to predict foreseeable misuse or failure modes. These evaluations can inform upstream model providers, or inform supplementary mitigations by the deployer.
2801	RISK-169	A0955_Gipiškis2024	Benchmarks for Situational Awareness	Testing & Auditing	A model is situationally aware if it internally represents that it is a machine learning model and if it can accurately infer or act on model-relevant facts - e.g., if it is currently in training, testing, evaluation or deployment, or the desired outcome of an evaluation. Some benchmarks exist for situational awareness of AI models, which test whether the AI models can classify stereotypical inputs from training, test- ing, evaluation and deployment as such, and whether the AI model can use this information correctly to take actions in the world [25, 111].
