11723	RISK-33	A0777_UK Government2023	Adaptation of Mitigations for Unintended Model Use	Risk Management	Adapt mitigations in recognition of risks from unintended model use or use in unexpected contexts, such as a model that is modified to remove safeguards after open- sourcing or a model that is combined with another model for unanticipated purposes. For example, at a given risk threshold, information security control mitigations might be put in place before even internal use of a model within a frontier AI organisation. In general, the use of caution may be helpful, given current limitations in information security controls and the prediction of models’ emergent abilities.
