7404	RISK-41	A0943_Gipiškis2024	Red teaming to test the resilience of open-weights models to fine-tuning	Testing & Auditing	Before the release of open-weights models, red teamers can test the resilience of safety training against fine-tuning. Safety training may be partially or fully overridden by fine-tuning intentionally (e.g., by malicious actors) or uninten- tionally (e.g., by fine tuning an AI model for a specific use case)
1460	RISK-414	A0955_Gipiškis2024	Benchmarks for Situational Awareness	Testing & Auditing	A model is situationally aware if it internally represents that it is a machine learning model and if it can accurately infer or act on model-relevant facts - e.g., if it is currently in training, testing, evaluation or deployment, or the desired outcome of an evaluation. Some benchmarks exist for situational awareness of AI models, which test whether the AI models can classify stereotypical inputs from training, test- ing, evaluation and deployment as such, and whether the AI model can use this information correctly to take actions in the world [25, 111].
14554	RISK-410	A0709_NIST2024	Harmful Bias and Homogenization Data Review	Data Governance	Review, document, and measure sources of bias in GAI training and TEVV data:Differences in distributions of outcomes across and within groups, includingintersecting groups; Completeness, representativeness, and balance of datasources; demographic group and subgroup coverage in GAI system trainingdata; Forms of latent systemic bias in images, text, audio, embeddings, or othercomplex or unstructured data; Input data features that may serve as proxies fordemographic group membership (i.e., image metadata, language dialect) orotherwise give rise to emergent bias within GAI systems; The extent to whichthe digital divide may negatively impact representativeness in GAI systemtraining and TEVV data; Filtering of hate speech or content in GAI systemtraining data; Prevalence of GAI-generated data in GAI system training data
