10282	RISK-609	A0949_Gipiškis2024	Testing for erroneous or irrelevant features through concept learning	Testing & Auditing	Interpretability techniques, particularly concept learning [77], can be used to test whether a model is learning erroneous features or relying on irrelevant features in its predictions. This can help identify and mitigate potential risks associated with incorrect or non-informative features influencing the model’s outputs.
