7907	RISK-684	A0938_Gipiškis2024	Calibrated confidence measures for model pre- dictions	System Documentation	Incorporating calibrated confidence measures alongside a model’s predictions and standard performance metrics, such as accuracy, can help users identify in- stances of overconfidence in incorrect predictions or underconfidence in correct ones [85]. These additional measures can provide users with more information to better interpret the model’s decisions and assess whether its predictions can be trusted.
7908	RISK-684	A0863_UK Government2023	Cost-Benefit Analysis of Sharing Vulnerability Reports	Risk Disclosure	Consider the ways in which sharing information about vulnerabilities can both exacerbate and mitigate risks. Sharing can alert would-be attackers, but also alert would-be victims and actors with the power to create defences. One particularly important factor is how easily fixable the model vulnerability is. If a vulnerability will take a very long time to fix, or cannot be fixed, then public reporting may not be justified.
